      "content": "I'll read the original test and CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now let me look at the base class to understand `checkEncodingVariations` and `getStringEncoder`.Now I have a clear picture. I'll write an improved version with:\n1. A named constant for the expected code to make sharing explicit\n2. Inline comments explaining *why* each assertion exists\n3. Grouping the name variations visually by phonetic pattern\n4. A cleaner Javadoc that explains the H/W rule more precisely\n5. Only the imports that are actually usedThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `SoundexTest_testHWRuleEx3.java` is complete — it extracts the shared expected code into a named constant, adds clear inline comments explaining the H/W rule for each assertion, visually groups the surname variations by phonetic pattern, and tightens the Javadoc to precisely describe what the rule means and why the test exists."
